            "privateNotes": "",
            "publicNotes": "<p>Thashes are elementals that escaped the Plane of Earth millennia ago and now wander the wilds of Sekamina. Resembling ankylosauruses with two tails—one at its back end, and one where its head should be—thashes have no traditional sensory organs. Rather, they experience the world solely through the vibrations they sense in the ground beneath their feet.</p>\n<p>Armored in stone and equipped with two smashing tails, thashes are fearless, attacking any creature that wanders into their territory, including other thashes. Since they're inedible, ornery, and not smart enough to have a self-preservation instinct, most Darklands predators avoid them. The only creatures that don't fear thashes are cavern trolls and other rock-eaters, as well as ayindilar elves and the other Darklands cultures who've learned to train them as tireless (if unpredictable) beasts of burden.</p><h2>Beasts of Burden</h2><p>Although difficult to train, thashes are both tireless and strong, features that make them excellent beasts of burden for those who know how to control them. Thashes find the vibration of footsteps irresistible. Though a creature that approaches a thash is likely to get their head caved in, a thash will follow anything that keeps a steady pace some distance ahead of them. Difficulty arises only when the time comes to load or unload the thash: cargo and passengers are typically lowered onto the creature's back from above.</p>",
            "publication": {
                "license": "ORC",
                "remaster": true,
                "title": "Pathfinder Adventure Path #225: Vaultlines"
            }
        },
